WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.488
Lab 2 connects one real server.

2
00:00:02.488 --> 00:00:06.871
You need a commercial test subscription
in the GCC tenant, a Linux server

3
00:00:06.871 --> 00:00:11.475
you can rebuild, never production, and
a control node with a managed identity.

4
00:00:11.475 --> 00:00:13.240
Create a test resource group,

5
00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:18.535
and grant the control node's managed identity
the Azure Connected Machine Onboarding

6
00:00:18.535 --> 00:00:20.152
role on it, and nothing else;

7
00:00:20.152 --> 00:00:24.050
that's the role Microsoft Learn's
Ansible onboarding page names.

8
00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:28.162
Write a one-server CMDB export
for the disposable server.

9
00:00:28.162 --> 00:00:33.788
Then plan, dry-run and connect it, and
check that its tags equal the CMDB's.

10
00:00:33.788 --> 00:00:38.624
To back it out, follow the order in Learn's
pages on azcmagent disconnect and on

11
00:00:38.624 --> 00:00:41.571
uninstalling the agent:
remove any extensions,

12
00:00:41.571 --> 00:00:45.954
disconnect with an identity that
may delete the resource, because the

13
00:00:45.954 --> 00:00:50.563
onboarding role can't, uninstall the
agent, and remove the role assignment.

14
00:00:50.563 --> 00:00:52.712
The authors haven't run Lab 2.

15
00:00:52.712 --> 00:00:56.110
Follow Chapter 08's Lab 2, step by step.
